1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,520
Three food coma myths keep tricking you every day.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:05,920
Save this before your next lunch.

3
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:10,240
Myth: it's the tryptophan in turkey putting you to sleep.

4
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:16,160
Fact: researchers say tryptophan alone rarely explains real drowsiness.

5
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:24,960
It's the carb-heavy, oversized meal built around it, spiking your blood sugar, then crashing it, that actually does the damage.

6
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,160
Myth: you're just tired from your morning.

7
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:36,400
Fact: a high-fat meal triggers your immune system to release cytokines, small proteins tied to fatigue.

8
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:42,320
Fried food and heavy sauces set this off, on top of whatever your blood sugar is doing.

9
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:46,320
Myth: you just need more willpower to push through.

10
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:56,160
Fact: your body clock dips between two and four in the afternoon, the same low point your brain hits overnight, just twelve hours later.

11
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:59,120
Lunch just lands right in the middle of it.

12
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:08,880
Lead your plate with protein and fiber, keep the fried and heavy stuff to a smaller portion, and eat until satisfied, not stuffed.

13
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:18,000
For the two o'clock dip specifically, a short nap before two, or a few minutes in bright light, helps reset your alertness.
